 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Wallpaper became the enthusiast kind with 17 archetypes (Morris & Co., Cole & Son, Scalamandré, Zuber, Timorous Beasties, Lincrusta, Anaglypta, plus maker-free Chinese wallpaper and Toile de Jouy); mass-market Arthouse/Holden/Rasch/Superfresco models kept as m. Wickes own-label tile ranges (Cosmopolitan, Farmhouse, Metro; Central Park, Lava, Livingstone, Melia, Onyx, Petra, Ruben, Sigford) are blank-maker names: folded into types (metro etc.) and dropped as models; no tile brands added (no tier research done). Left out: Florence Broadhurst (no named design confirmed on a fetched page), Morris Golden Lily/Snakeshead (only retailer search snippets), de Gournay Earlham and Glasgow Toile original date (pages 403 or undated), Cole & Son Woods designer. Heritage tiles belong to Heritage & reclaimed."
}